{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change","id":1124961,"title":"Garou Embraced before First Change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-04T14:58:47-07:00","id":1124961,"title":"Garou Embraced before First Change","content":"If by chance (or complex design) a Garou were to be embraced before they underwent the First Change (the True Black Hand often kidnaps and indoctrinates children before the embrace, these are known as Chatterlings, and it is not unknown for them to attack and embrace Werewolves, just as example), would they become an Abomination?<br /> <br /> Before the First Change a Werewolf presumably doesn't possess a Gnosis trait, making them a prime target for embrace. Would they undergo the First Change after their Embrace? Would they be locked in a pre-Change state?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T16:00:04-07:00","id":1124990,"title":"","content":"They would become abominations, you are born a garou after all. They would have their First Change when they were embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T16:22:49-07:00","id":1124997,"title":"","content":"No, they would just not experience it because the Kindred blood would put them into stasis (it is similar to what happens when a pre-Change Garou is ghouled). In effect, they would be an aborted Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:06:13-07:00","id":1125006,"title":"","content":"See I see both sides of this.<br /> <br /> On the one hand an embraced Garou is an Abomination. On the other, the Embrace might leave them stuck in the state that comes before their awakening as Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:37:03-07:00","id":1125015,"title":"","content":"Before the first change they're only kinfolk, not garou. Take any werewolf: had he passed through the adolescence without stressful or traumatic events and reached 25 years, he wouldn't have suffered a first change and he never would again, remaining a kinfolk.<br /> Unless they were metis before the first change, in that case they would die. The chance of spawning an abomination is really, really low and most of the embraced Garou die in minutes.<br /> <br /> An embraced kinfolk is going to be just a vampire, maybe with some particular background that gives him connection with the Garou society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T17:55:01-07:00","id":1125024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125015#post1125015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the first change they're only kinfolk, not garou. Take any werewolf: had he passed through the adolescence without stressful or traumatic events and reached 25 years, he wouldn't have suffered a first change and he never would again, remaining a kinfolk.<br /> Unless they were metis before the first change, in that case they would die. The chance of spawning an abomination is really, really low and most of the embraced Garou die in minutes.<br /> <br /> An embraced kinfolk is going to be just a vampire, maybe with some particular background that gives him connection with the Garou society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well with a Gnosis of 1 it's a 1/10 chance of becoming a Vampire; they only undergo a full Embrace if they Botch the roll. Failure means an agonizing, slow death. Success means peacefully drifting off...<br /> <br /> Okay, that makes sense. Since they're Kinfolk until the first change, that puts a different light on things. With that said I would argue that the Embrace is a traumatic experience that could, in and of itself, trigger the Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:15:13-07:00","id":1125033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125024#post1125024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well with a Gnosis of 1 it's a 1/10 chance of becoming a Vampire; they only undergo a full Embrace if they Botch the roll. Failure means an agonizing, slow death. Success means peacefully drifting off...</div> </div> </div> </div>Afaik kiss and embrace are usually quite ecstatic experiences for humans (Giovanni aside), and surely won't trigger anything if done with the victim asleep. But even more so, First Change means frenzy and should one be triggered during an Embrace the vampire is then probably taken by surprise and dead in the first round.<br /> <br /> Garou also have no Gnosis rating before the first change (okay they could, still wouldn't spawn an abomination), except for the usual Metis garou (that has three).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:18:22-07:00","id":1125036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125015#post1125015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the first change they're only kinfolk, not garou. Take any werewolf: had he passed through the adolescence without stressful or traumatic events and reached 25 years, he wouldn't have suffered a first change and he never would again, remaining a kinfolk.<br /> Unless they were metis before the first change, in that case they would die. The chance of spawning an abomination is really, really low and most of the embraced Garou die in minutes.<br /> <br /> An embraced kinfolk is going to be just a vampire, maybe with some particular background that gives him connection with the Garou society.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect; Garou are definitely Garou before their change and not Kinfolk. Metis are born from older pre-change Garou thinking that they're kin, and I recall KABA giving a guideline where you roll the starting Gnosis for the breed if this sort of thing happens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T19:32:31-07:00","id":1125053,"title":"","content":"First thing first... what does KABA stands for? Is it a manual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T20:05:59-07:00","id":1125063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125053#post1125053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First thing first... what does KABA stands for? Is it a manual?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk: A Breed Apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T21:09:20-07:00","id":1125081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125036#post1125036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is incorrect; Garou are definitely Garou before their change and not Kinfolk. Metis are born from older pre-change Garou thinking that they're kin, and I recall KABA giving a guideline where you roll the starting Gnosis for the breed if this sort of thing happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, werewolves before the first change would seem like kinfolk, but the first change will necessarily happen eventually. I would expect a vampiric Embrace to trigger a first change; if it doesn't, that's probably proof the person was only ever kinfolk, not truly a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:30:47-07:00","id":1125270,"title":"","content":"Okay, I thank you for the specification, I admit I totally missed that this supplement was even published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T11:33:00-07:00","id":1125970,"title":"","content":"Ignoring semantics of the proper name for the new vampire, the real question is whether the vampire has the powers of the Garou. I would say no. It's like asking if a newly embraced caterpillar will become a vampire butterfly - biological processes stop upon death. At the time of the embrace, the pre-Change Garou cannot shapechange and does not have Rage or Gnosis. I see no reason why these powers would automatically happen.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, mechanically there is the issue of Gnosis. A pre-Change vampire doesn't have any. An Abomination cannot increase Gnosis at all. I don't think you can have a Garou without Gnosis.<br /> <br /> It is entirely possible that an assault by the vampire would trigger the First Change (in which case the survival of the vampire is called into question), but that would not be automatic and I can think all sorts of scenarios where that likely would not happen. A direct physical attack could well trigger a Garou's First Change. But I think it is less likely if it happens during the course of a seduction or while the victim is sleeping. This would be an ST ruling in an individual chronicle, not some obvious rule for STs to use in a standard game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:25:49-07:00","id":1125989,"title":"","content":"Yes, it would be appropriate if the First Change occurred due to the potential Garou being attacked by a Sabbat pack instead of it occurring while interacting with Mortals or Kinfolk. I imagine that the resulting Garou would be relatively well balanced, as they would see their transformation into one of the Garou as being a source of strength rather than a process that alienated/killed people that they cared about. It would also be a good backstory that could be used to explain a truckload of unusual Abilities, Backgrounds, Flaws, and/or Merits. For example, such a Garou would be justified to take Allies (Vampire Hunters), Lore (Kindred), Untamable, and Vengeful (Sabbat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T13:13:23-07:00","id":1126011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125989#post1125989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it would be appropriate if the First Change occurred due to the potential Garou being attacked by a Sabbat pack instead of it occurring while interacting with Mortals or Kinfolk. I imagine that the resulting Garou would be relatively well balanced, as they would see their transformation into one of the Garou as being a source of strength rather than a process that alienated/killed people that they cared about. It would also be a good backstory that could be used to explain a truckload of unusual Abilities, Backgrounds, Flaws, and/or Merits. For example, such a Garou would be justified to take Allies (Vampire Hunters), Lore (Kindred), Untamable, and Vengeful (Sabbat).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting way to have a fairly guilt-free First Change! One young Garou to another: &quot;Wow. I'm sorry to hear about your family. The first thing I ever did as a werewolf was kill a leech.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T07:46:14-07:00","id":1126307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1125970#post1125970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring semantics of the proper name for the new vampire, the real question is whether the vampire has the powers of the Garou. I would say no. It's like asking if a newly embraced caterpillar will become a vampire butterfly - biological processes stop upon death. At the time of the embrace, the pre-Change Garou cannot shapechange and does not have Rage or Gnosis. I see no reason why these powers would automatically happen.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, mechanically there is the issue of Gnosis. A pre-Change vampire doesn't have any. An Abomination cannot increase Gnosis at all. I don't think you can have a Garou without Gnosis.<br /> <br /> It is entirely possible that an assault by the vampire would trigger the First Change (in which case the survival of the vampire is called into question), but that would not be automatic and I can think all sorts of scenarios where that likely would not happen. A direct physical attack could well trigger a Garou's First Change. But I think it is less likely if it happens during the course of a seduction or while the victim is sleeping. This would be an ST ruling in an individual chronicle, not some obvious rule for STs to use in a standard game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that, per KABA and textual evidence from before it, everything indicates that pre-Change Garou do have Rage and Gnosis prior to their First Change, because they always have some nagging feeling of there being more (latent spiritual awareness = influence of having Gnosis), and they are also angry enough that others shy away from them (The Curse = Rage is apparent). When the books say that Garou are born Garou and not Kinfolk, they mean it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:02:53-07:00","id":1126709,"title":"","content":"I do a simple House Rule.<br /> <br /> 1. Garou die during the Embrace, no abominations.<br /> <br /> 2. Garou become vampires and lose all their previous powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T20:27:51-07:00","id":1127902,"title":"","content":"I usually play Theurges and in the Theurge information across various books but predominantly in Book of Auspices, they always know something isn't quite the same with them compared to everyone else. And their first change is typically easier than other auspices because they've had that connection. This to me would indicate that the Gnosis is there pre-change. Otherwise, you would end up with kinfolk spontaneously going through first change if there's no rage or gnosis latent within them.<br /> <br /> So I think it's a good bet to say that any pre-change Garou who is embraced would end up dead or an abomination. And I would typically NPC an abomination unless the game is centred around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13401-quoth","name":"Quoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13401_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T22:33:45-07:00","id":1127925,"title":"","content":"I actually played pretty much this exact concept once, a pre-change Garou caught in a Sabbat mass embrace. He nearly died because even unchanged the embrace didn't want to take, and by the time he clawed his way out of the earth the pack had already taken their shovel heads and left the rest for dead. The result was a Caitiff who happened to have Protean with the flaws Lunacy and Vulnerable to Silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T01:41:16-07:00","id":1127975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1127925#post1127925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually played pretty much this exact concept once, a pre-change Garou caught in a Sabbat mass embrace. He nearly died because even unchanged the embrace didn't want to take, and by the time he clawed his way out of the earth the pack had already taken their shovel heads and left the rest for dead. The result was a Caitiff who happened to have Protean with the flaws Lunacy and Vulnerable to Silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you use the Abomination rules? So did they get the Forms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:17:22-07:00","id":1128012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1127975#post1127975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you use the Abomination rules? So did they get the Forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know in which Wt:A books there are rules for Garou Abominations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T08:35:25-07:00","id":1128056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128012#post1128012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know in which Wt:A books there are rules for Garou Abominations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Under A Blood Red Moon, 2nd Edition Player's Guide, Revised Storyteller's Handbook, W20 Changing Breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T08:57:02-07:00","id":1128061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1127975#post1127975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you use the Abomination rules? So did they get the Forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They were just a Caitiff with an odd werewolf-y discipline and werewolf-y flaws. Basically a shadow of what they might have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T09:08:48-07:00","id":1128067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128061#post1128061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. They were just a Caitiff with an odd werewolf-y discipline and werewolf-y flaws. Basically a shadow of what they might have been.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly I prefer this and the Kyasd Dark ages solution for &quot;crossover&quot; embraces. Good chance of failure and a you get something wierd but not &quot;I have to have two games worth of material to play&quot; ,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T02:05:41-07:00","id":1128366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128012#post1128012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know in which Wt:A books there are rules for Garou Abominations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally dislike the W20 take, so here's mine.<br /> <br /> Gnosis, Rage, Primal Urge, Gifts etc. are gone. If there isn't space for it on a Vampire sheet, it's gone.<br /> <br /> Forms are kept but you transform using Blood. All of the benefits of the forms stay except for the healing factor of Crinos form.<br /> <br /> NPC Abominations may possess a merit where they can heal Aggravated damage (I do this to make them uniquely terrifying, since very few beings possess this ability) as though it were Lethal.<br /> <br /> They can no longer enter the Umbra.<br /> <br /> They may possess the traits of their Clan, however a relatively high proportion become Caitiff since their body naturally rejects the blood; even if the Embrace works it may not work fully.<br /> <br /> They suffer a weakness to Silver, which inflicts Aggravated damage on them.<br /> <br /> They are at +2 difficulty to all Self-Control rolls. As a result of this, many become Diablerie addicts.<br /> <br /> They do not regain Willpower from resting, and many develop a severe Depression not unlike Harano. Many commit suicide (after exacting revenge on their Sire and any Vampires they can get their hands on). Many die alone, since they do not want their tribe to see what they became in their final hours. Those who remain alive typically do so because of Rotschrek; they simply aren't strong enough to face Helios's embrace. So they kid themselves that they will carry on to kill a few more leeches... and the days become weeks and the weeks become years, and eventually they are one of the monsters they once fought.<br /> <br /> I personally dislike the VtM rules that state they can't regain Humanity or Willpower with EXP, and other stuff that damns them from day 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:16:18-07:00","id":1128436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128366#post1128366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forms are kept but you transform using Blood. All of the benefits of the forms stay except for the healing factor of Crinos form.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Crinos has no special healing factor; that's a function of being a Garou and outside of your breed form, or simply being Metis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally dislike the VtM rules that state they can't regain Humanity or Willpower with EXP, and other stuff that damns them from day 1. </div> </div> </div>They shouldn't have Humanity. Even Homid Garou were never actually human to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:08:56-07:00","id":1128536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128436#post1128436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Crinos has no special healing factor; that's a function of being a Garou and outside of your breed form, or simply being Metis.<br /> <br /> They shouldn't have Humanity. Even Homid Garou were never actually human to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Ah, my mistake. Well they can only heal with Blood regardless.<br /> <br /> - Hmm... I could see them having a Path of Morality which reflects the nature of Garou, but fundamentally Humanity isn't about your beliefs. If you're embraced, even as a sociopath whose beliefs PERFECTLY line up with the superficial ethics of the Path of Power and the Inner Voice, you default to Humanity... probably low Humanity. Garou who are embraced lose their spirit side and are effectively an abominable combination of things that shouldn't mix, so them being shunted onto Humanity (a metric of Not At All Like the Beast down to Exactly Like the Beast) makes sense for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T14:39:11-07:00","id":1128578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128436#post1128436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They shouldn't have Humanity. Even Homid Garou were never actually human to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity has nothing to do with BEING human its all about ACTING human. A Garou is more likely to instinctively know how to pretend to be human than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T16:34:24-07:00","id":1128611,"title":"","content":"No, in cWoD, Humanity is about being human, not acting human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T05:22:10-07:00","id":1128767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128611#post1128611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, in cWoD, Humanity is about being human, not acting human.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books have always been a tad... odd on this. Sometimes it's about seeming human, sometimes it's about feeling human, sometimes it's about being human, sometimes it's about NOT being the beast.<br /> <br /> So any take is correct until the VtM line 100% settles what it means and STICKS with it for a whole edition. V20 isn't consistent on this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T06:39:11-07:00","id":1128784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128611#post1128611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, in cWoD, Humanity is about being human, not acting human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then no kindred should ever have it. <br /> <br /> <br /> In Requiem Humanity about how human you are. AT higher ends of it you take less damage from the sun and are less bound by your vampiric nature. In Requiem you lose humanity not just by doing things that are wicked but things that aren't human that are of debate neutral.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade Humanity is one of many moral paths that kindred use to fight off the Beast it is the most &quot;natural one&quot; because it &quot;try to pretend to be human&quot; and kindred generally have had life time of being human to work from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T07:57:55-07:00","id":1128820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128784#post1128784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then no kindred should ever have it.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Requiem Humanity about how human you are. AT higher ends of it you take less damage from the sun and are less bound by your vampiric nature. In Requiem you lose humanity not just by doing things that are wicked but things that aren't human that are of debate neutral.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade Humanity is one of many moral paths that kindred use to fight off the Beast it is the most &quot;natural one&quot; because it &quot;try to pretend to be human&quot; and kindred generally have had life time of being human to work from.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Kindred have Humanity because it's a residue that they can either try to scrub off or try to keep with utmost dedication. But Garou don't have this residual humanity, as they are all born with Rage and Gnosis and their struggles in life don't set them up for denial of what they are, as opposed to vampires turned into humans later in life..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T05:09:52-07:00","id":1129186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1124961-garou-embraced-before-first-change?p=1128820#post1128820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Kindred have Humanity because it's a residue that they can either try to scrub off or try to keep with utmost dedication. But Garou don't have this residual humanity, as they are all born with Rage and Gnosis and their struggles in life don't set them up for denial of what they are, as opposed to vampires turned into humans later in life..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No they don't. Humanity is no more a residue than Path of Paradox. Its an instinctive construct to combat the beast since the Kindred spent most of their life being human. It is intrinsically artificial thus why its so important as part of the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}